From c88e489893291472eed0cc9dd7e9f5417f4a38dc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tong <zhengtong0611@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 06:05:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 09/13] Referee bridge: dance music switch and auto-stop
 (verdict dances)

The debate server's DebateResult has each side bot dance after the
verdict: the winner's with its music, the loser's in silence, both for
dance_s. So "dance" now also reads "on" (play the dance's music) and
"seconds" (stop after this long; 0 = to the end), both in SpeechCmd.

on=true sets the dance player's AudioSource to danceMusicVolume, a new
speech_bridge.json key (default 0.4; ME's own dance volume is 0.5 and no
pet/effects/menu volume setting reaches it); on=false sets it to 0. With
seconds > 0 a timer stops the dance, and the title loops until then
instead of going on to the next installed dance. A later dance, a
dance_stop, or a say that stops the dance cancels the timer. Once the
dance is over, however it ended, the player's own volume and loop
setting come back. The volume is set before PlayIndex, which starts the
music within the call when the avatar is already idle.

Older servers send neither key, and JsonUtility cannot tell a missing
field from false/0. A server that knows the extension sends "seconds"
with every command, so a batch without a "seconds": key is an older
server, and its dance plays as before: player volume, to the end.

Logs: the dance line says music on/volume or silent and the stop time,
"dancing: ... playing=True volume=0.40 loop=True" once it plays, then
"dance stopped after N s" and "dance over; dance volume back to 0.50".
