+### Extension: `on` and `seconds` on `dance` (verdict dances)
+
+Added for the debate's verdict, in the server's `docs/INTEGRATION.md`:
+
+```
+Cmd = {"op":"say"|"talk"|"stop"|"dance"|"dance_stop","id":"","text":"","audio":"","title":"","on":false,"clear":false,"seconds":0}
+- dance also carries on (play the dance's music; false = silent) and seconds (stop after this long; 0 = play
+  to the end). Older builds ignore both and play with their configured volume to the end.
+- Verdict dances. On the for and against channels, DebateResult becomes dance with title=dances[channel],
+  on=music[channel], seconds=dance_s, and SessionStart also sends dance_stop.
+```
+
+So after a debate the winner's side bot dances with its music and the loser's dances in silence, both for `dance_s`.
+The titles carry the joke ("MMD-Conqueror", "MMD-Lost One_s Weeping"; on a draw "MMD-皆大欢喜-卜逻desu"); the motions
+are ordinary upbeat dances. A later upgrade could use Mixamo "Victory" and "Defeated" clips instead, exported as
+dance mods with `DanceModCli` (below) and named in the server's `JUDGE_DANCE_WIN` / `JUDGE_DANCE_LOSE`.
+
+**Older servers.** `JsonUtility` reads a missing field as `false` or `0`, so on its own a `dance` from a server that
+predates this extension would look like "silent, to the end". The bridge therefore looks at the whole response: a
+server that sends `seconds` sends it with every command, so a batch without any `"seconds":` key comes from an older
+server, and its `dance` plays exactly as before (at the dance player's own volume, to the end; `on` is ignored). A
+server that knows the extension must send `on: true` for any dance it wants heard, the operator's included.
+
